    <h1 class="font-bold text-xl">About me</h1>

    <p><strong>Hello!</strong> I am a <strong>software engineer</strong> (and occasional <strong>systems administrator</strong>) who loves getting her hands dirty with both new and old technologies alike.</p>

    <p>My professional experience generally leans towards <strong>full stack web development</strong> with a <strong>hint of DevOps</strong> but I have also worked on personal projects ranging the gamut from <strong>native desktop development</strong> (including some bare metal assembly development), <strong>game development</strong> and even a bit of <strong>hardware and embedded development</strong>. I have a particular passion for retrocomputing and vintage hardware and enjoy learning the ins and outs of systems of the 70's and 80's.</p>

    <p>My talents include a mastery of programming languages such as <strong>C</strong>, <strong>C#</strong>, <strong>PHP</strong>, <strong>JavaScript</strong>, <strong>SQL</strong>, <strong>Python</strong>, <strong>Bash</strong>, and <strong>Lua</strong> in addition to technologies such as <strong>Node.js</strong>, <strong>React</strong>, <strong>Laravel</strong>, <strong>Windows Server</strong> and <strong>Linux</strong>, among many others.</p>

    <p>Of course, I'm always looking for new and interesting technologies to learn and innovate with!</p>
